---
description: Git usage and commits
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not run git commands or make git-related changes unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not create commits unless the user explicitly asks you to commit.
- Write a precise commit subject line that explains the change on its own.
- Avoid a commit body when the subject is enough.
- If a body is needed, keep it as short as possible.
- Do not add Co-Authored-By, "collaboration with", or other AI attribution to commits or PR descriptions.
